<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heraios</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE–1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heraios was a ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> known only from his coins, which were inscribed in Greek and show him in Hellenistic royal style with a steppe-style portrait. He probably reigned in the late 1st century BCE or early 1st century CE and was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a> lords; his coins call him a Kushan, but his relation to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kujula-kadphises">Kujula Kadphises</a> is uncertain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraios.jpg" alt="Heraios" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heraios_coin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
